, or market prices are yet available for this race, leaving fundamentals to carry the forecast.\n\nThe main in-state storyline concerns Gov. Josh Shapiro, who polls show with a wide lead in his reelection bid and a place among national Democratic frontrunners, though Pennsylvania voters are split on whether they want him to run for president. His presence atop the Democratic ticket could narrow the state's slight Republican tilt, but until nominees and polling take shape, the race sits as a genuine tossup with a hair-thin Republican edge.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.4565, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.5269, "margin": 0.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.504, "margin": 0.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.475, "margin": -0.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.4803, "margin": -0.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.5405, "margin": 1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.485, "margin": -0.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.4847, "margin": -0.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.4588, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.4605, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.5147, "margin": 0.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.4565, "margin": -1.0}]}